  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Line joining the midpoints of two sides is <math><mo>&#8741;</mo></math> to the third side and half of it.<br /><math><mi>&#8736;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mn>90</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">o</mi></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;(as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mo>&#8869;</mo><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi></math>)<br />Hence <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">P</mi></math> will be the orthocentre<br /><img src=\"assets\\st0107_883c9ceeca65.png\" style=\"height: 152px; width: 260px;\" /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>O</mi><mi>B</mi><mi>P</mi></math>&nbsp;forms a rectangle.</p><p><math><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>&#160;</mi><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>A</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>O</mi></math>&nbsp;(using the concept that diagonals bisect&nbsp;each other)<br /><br /><math><mi>P</mi><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mi>&#160;</mi><mfenced close=\"\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtable><mtr><mtd><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>5</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mfenced></math></p>"
  }
